message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the associated paper."
title: "Approximate Stationary Analysis and Empirical Verification of Noise-Resilient Cooperation in the Iterated Prisoner's Dilemma"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kushalk0677/Closed-Form-Stationary-Analysis-and-Empirical-Verification-of-Noise-Resilient-Cooperation"
license: MIT
year: 2025
abstract: >
  Source code, simulation data, and figures for a study introducing NAFT
  (Noisy Adaptive Forgiving Tit-for-Tat), a memory-1 strategy with controlled
  stochastic forgiveness designed to maintain cooperative stability under
  execution noise in the Iterated Prisoner's Dilemma. Includes Markov chain
  stationary analysis, Monte Carlo simulations, and evolutionary dynamics.
keywords:
  - iterated prisoner's dilemma
  - cooperation
  - Markov chains
  - Tit-for-Tat
  - forgiveness
  - evolutionary game theory
  - multi-agent systems
  - noise resilience
